  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given circuit the R.M.S. values of voltages across the capacitor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, inductor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> and resistor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> respectively. Then the peak voltage across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0009_3f0c501357b1.jpg\" style=\"width: 190px; height: 318px;\" /></p>\r"
